{title: 330 - Take My Life and Let It Be}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #330 • HENDON • 14.14.7}
{lyricist: Frances Ridley Havergal}
{composer: H. A. Cesar Malan}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 330}
{meta: tune HENDON}
{meta: meter 14.14.7}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Take my [Am]life, and let it [F]be Consecrated, [Bb]Lord, [Gm]to Thee;
[F/C]Take my [C]hands, and [C7]let them [F/C]move [Am]At the impulse [C7]of Thy [F/C]love;
[Dm/A]At [C]the [F/C]impulse [Bb]of [Dm/A]Thylove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]Take [Am]my feet, [F]and let [Bb]them [Gm]be
[Dm/A]Swift [Am]and beautiful [Bb]for [Gm]Thee.
[F/C]Take [C]my [C7]voice, [F/C]and [Am]let [C7]me sing
[Dm/A]Always, [F/C]only, [Bb]for [Dm/A]my [C/G]King;
[Dm/A]Always, [F/C]only, [Bb]for [Dm/A]my [C/G]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Take [Am]my lips, [F]and let [Bb]them [Gm]be
[Dm/A]Filled [Am]with messages [Bb]from [Gm]Thee.
[F/C]Take [C]my [C7]silver [Am]and [C7]my gold:
[Dm/A]Not [C]a [F/C]mite [Bb]would I [Dm/A]withhold;
[Dm/A]Not [C]a [F/C]mite [Bb]would I [Dm/A]withhold.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Take [Am]my will, [F]and make [Bb]it [Gm]Thine,
[Dm/A]It [Am]shall be [F]no longer [Gm]mine;
[F/C]Take [C]my [C7]heart, [F/C]it [Am]is [C7]Thine own,
[Dm/A]It [C]shall [F/C]be [Bb]Thy [Dm/A]royal [C/G]throne.
[Dm/A]It [C]shall [F/C]be [Bb]Thy [Dm/A]royal [C/G]throne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm/A]Take [Am]my love, [F]my Lord, [Bb]I [Gm]pour
[Dm/A]At [Am]Thy feet [F]its treasure [Gm]store;
[F/C]Take [C]myself, [F/C]and [Am]I [C7]will be,
[Dm/A]Ever, [F/C]only, [Bb]all [Dm/A]for [C/G]Thee.
[Dm/A]Ever, [F/C]only, [Bb]all [Dm/A]for [C/G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
